From bb5f79435e72742d5de8b35d0a2f763ba4f7f0c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 10:04:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 179/180] patch 0179 -- frame-spike detector + fire-dispatch
 path bracket (v1.0.3 clean re-author)

Clean re-author of the SFXPAUSE-010 frame-spike + firepath probes,
kept as useful no-window perf diagnostics.

Two independent gates (both default OFF):
- SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FRAME_SPIKE_DETECT=1: emits [frame-spike]
  inter_ms=M whenever the inter-frame wall delta in run_tick_fixed
  exceeds 50 ms. NO fixed window -- session-wide. The no-window form
  that caught the fire-frame stall all the frame-30-windowed probes
  missed.
- SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FIREPATH_TRACE=1: emits [firepath] func=NAME
  wall_us=N on the FIRST call per session of FireWeapon (p_arms.cpp),
  CreateBullet (ObjManager.cpp), effect (caret.cpp), ai_polar_shot
  (ai/weapons/polar_mgun.cpp). Per-function static-bool _seen flag
  gated on the probe.

main.cpp exports firepath_trace_active() extern "C"; the 4 consumer
TUs declare it at file scope. Clean-stack note: run_tick_fixed
contains ONLY the frame-spike entry check -- the dropped campaign
catch-up/first_tick/per-tick/yield brackets are GONE.

Both default OFF -> production byte-identical to golden.
Workspace-local; never upstreamed.
